WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.370
Oh no! Oh no! An unexpected person
has come from the spirit world!

00:00:04.570 --> 00:00:06.870
His name is Izumi Lio,
and he came because

00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:10.530
the Division Chief of Death Spirits told him
to make sure we were doing our jobs.

00:00:11.470 --> 00:00:15.230
What'll we do if they find out that we've
been transforming Mitsuki into Full Moon?!

00:00:15.470 --> 00:00:17.000
We were able to
fool them this time,

00:00:17.030 --> 00:00:19.870
but I get a bad feeling
we'll be caught sometime soon!

00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:23.170
So, I wonder what's going to
happen today...

00:00:27.870 --> 00:00:28.900
Got that?

00:00:29.270 --> 00:00:29.930
Yes.

00:02:03.130 --> 00:02:05.670
<i>Well, our song of the day is</i>
<i>the one that rose</i>

00:02:05.700 --> 00:02:07.970
<i>to the top of the charts for</i>
<i>the first time this week,</i>

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:10.270
<i>Full Moon's "Eternal Snow"!</i>

00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:13.130
<i>This song is a cover song</i>
<i>of a masterpiece</i>

00:02:13.170 --> 00:02:16.000
<i>created by an 80's band</i>
<i>called "Route L,"</i>

00:02:16.030 --> 00:02:18.130
<i>and it is garnering quite</i>
<i>a lot of attention!</i>

00:02:18.230 --> 00:02:20.830
<i>This song targets</i>
<i>a wide range of ages.</i>

00:02:21.100 --> 00:02:22.930
<i>Let's see how well it does!</i>

00:02:23.130 --> 00:02:24.430
<i>Check it out!</i>

00:02:25.670 --> 00:02:27.500
"Hi Full Moon.
How are you doing?"

00:02:27.830 --> 00:02:30.770
"I went to buy your new single
the day it came out,"

00:02:30.800 --> 00:02:32.970
"but once I got home, I found out
that my mom had bought it too."

00:02:33.130 --> 00:02:35.800
"My mom and I are both
cheering for you!" this one says!

00:02:36.030 --> 00:02:37.530
Umm... This one says...

00:02:37.900 --> 00:02:40.100
Wow, this is from Nanami!

00:02:40.930 --> 00:02:44.030
<i>Full Moon, long time no see!</i>
<i>I bought "Eternal Snow."</i>

00:02:44.200 --> 00:02:45.930
<i>This song is also fantastic!</i>

00:02:45.970 --> 00:02:49.470
<i>There is no doubt about that because</i>
<i>I think so and I'm your number one fan!</i>

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:51.170
Thanks!

00:02:52.100 --> 00:02:56.830
But I can barely read all these,
let alone reply to them.

00:02:56.870 --> 00:02:59.030
Here! I'll help you with that!

00:02:59.070 --> 00:03:00.070
Stupid!

00:03:00.200 --> 00:03:02.930
You can't write them back!

00:03:02.970 --> 00:03:05.530
There, there. Anyway, this looks like
a pretty good start.

00:03:06.170 --> 00:03:09.070
Maybe this brought you closer
to finding Eichi.

00:03:09.200 --> 00:03:09.870
What?!

00:03:10.470 --> 00:03:12.100
Y-You think so?

00:03:12.130 --> 00:03:15.500
Oh, yeah! Maybe he'll come back
from America all of a sudden!

00:03:15.530 --> 00:03:17.270
What?! Oh my!

00:03:17.300 --> 00:03:20.970
Yeah! And you two will embrace each other
for the miraculous reunion!

00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:23.070
Mitsuki! Eichi!

00:03:24.130 --> 00:03:26.430
No, Meroko, stop it now!
Really!

00:03:43.400 --> 00:03:45.500
<i>That was Full Moon's</i>
<i>"Eternal Snow."</i>

00:03:57.970 --> 00:03:59.470
Excuse me, Ma'am.

00:04:01.300 --> 00:04:03.200
You have a visitor.

00:04:03.730 --> 00:04:04.730
Who is it?

00:04:05.200 --> 00:04:06.300
Well...

00:04:08.900 --> 00:04:10.830
Oh, Grandmother!

00:04:13.100 --> 00:04:14.870
I have not seen you in so long.

00:04:14.930 --> 00:04:18.200
Oh, please, don't be so formal!

00:04:18.330 --> 00:04:20.730
I'm so glad to see you again!

00:04:21.730 --> 00:04:22.400
Yes.

00:04:23.930 --> 00:04:25.800
Excuse me, Miss.

00:04:26.030 --> 00:04:28.070
Would you please take your shoes off?

00:04:29.470 --> 00:04:30.770
What?! To see me?

00:04:30.900 --> 00:04:33.900
Yes... She says she came all
the way from America.

00:04:34.070 --> 00:04:35.300
From America?

00:04:35.630 --> 00:04:36.630
Who could it be?

00:04:38.330 --> 00:04:42.930
From America, eh? Maybe it's Eichi!

00:04:43.330 --> 00:04:44.970
That's impossible!

00:04:46.570 --> 00:04:49.100
It's a souvenir for you.

00:04:50.530 --> 00:04:52.370
Here, please don't be so reserved!

00:04:52.570 --> 00:04:54.530
I think it suits you well, actually!

00:04:54.570 --> 00:04:55.700
Excuse me.

00:04:58.130 --> 00:04:59.500
Hi, Mitsuki!

00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:03.030
Oh, it was you, Ms. Kazumi!

00:05:03.270 --> 00:05:06.370
I was wondering who would
be visiting me from America.

00:05:06.430 --> 00:05:09.330
I am now married and living in America.

00:05:09.700 --> 00:05:11.070
Really?

00:05:11.100 --> 00:05:14.770
Oh, it's been two years!
How have you been?

00:05:15.600 --> 00:05:16.670
Hey, Mitsuki!

00:05:17.600 --> 00:05:18.270
Who's she?

00:05:18.330 --> 00:05:21.470
She's Ms. Kazumi, my teacher from
when I was in the orphanage.

00:05:22.070 --> 00:05:23.270
How disappointing.

00:05:28.130 --> 00:05:31.000
Ms. Kazumi, you're being dramatic.

00:05:31.670 --> 00:05:35.200
But I sure am glad you came
all the way to see me.

00:05:35.470 --> 00:05:38.730
I had to run some errands in Japan,
and when I was at the airport,

00:05:38.770 --> 00:05:41.530
I heard a song that
brought back memories.

00:05:41.570 --> 00:05:42.230
<i>A song?</i>

00:05:42.530 --> 00:05:45.530
Yes. The one that your father wrote,
"Eternal Snow."

00:05:45.670 --> 00:05:46.800
You remember it, right?

00:05:47.230 --> 00:05:48.330
Umm... Yeah...

00:05:53.300 --> 00:05:56.570
Hey! If you don't mind, why don't you
show me your room, Mitsuki!

00:05:56.870 --> 00:05:58.300
Is that all right?

00:05:59.030 --> 00:06:00.100
Well, sure.

00:06:00.500 --> 00:06:01.800
Okay. Then, let's go!

00:06:01.830 --> 00:06:03.230
Huh? Oh, yes!

00:06:10.400 --> 00:06:14.530
Yes, yes, this melody.
This is such a wonderful music box.

00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:17.800
This is a memento from my parents.

00:06:18.570 --> 00:06:19.570
Oh really?

00:06:20.330 --> 00:06:21.870
Ms. Kazumi, I'm sorry.

00:06:22.370 --> 00:06:24.770
My grandmother doesn't
really like music.

00:06:25.070 --> 00:06:28.300
No problem. I kind of sensed
that something was up.

00:06:28.700 --> 00:06:31.670
But weren't you dreaming
of becoming a singer?

00:06:32.000 --> 00:06:34.230
Yes! I haven't given up on that!

00:06:35.430 --> 00:06:36.930
Of course. Because...

00:06:37.270 --> 00:06:39.330
- "No one can get in the way of my dream!"
- "No one can get in the way of my dream!"

00:06:41.130 --> 00:06:44.400
You always said this to me back
when I was in the orphanage.

00:06:45.030 --> 00:06:46.630
You remembered?

00:06:46.800 --> 00:06:47.470
That's right!

00:06:47.730 --> 00:06:49.900
No one can get in
the way of dreams!

00:06:50.400 --> 00:06:53.200
<i>I'll definitely make Takuto</i>
<i>care about me!</i>

00:06:53.470 --> 00:06:55.300
Hey, what are you
thinking about right now?

00:06:55.470 --> 00:06:57.930
Are you curious about
what I am thinking?

00:06:58.130 --> 00:06:59.130
No.

00:07:01.230 --> 00:07:04.970
Oh, wasn't this calendar Eichi's?

00:07:05.230 --> 00:07:08.970
Oh, yes. I'm looking after it for him.

00:07:09.330 --> 00:07:10.500
Looking after it?

00:07:11.170 --> 00:07:11.830
<i>What?</i>

00:07:13.670 --> 00:07:16.630
<i>Eichi, is that true?</i>

00:07:17.430 --> 00:07:24.030
<i>Yes, I'm going to America with</i>
<i>my new dad and mom next week.</i>

00:07:25.100 --> 00:07:26.330
<i>America?</i>

00:07:26.930 --> 00:07:28.500
<i>I'm sorry for keeping it from you,</i>

00:07:28.800 --> 00:07:34.330
<i>but I wanted to tell it to you in person,</i>
<i>before I told everyone else.</i>

00:07:35.170 --> 00:07:36.300
<i>No way...</i>

00:07:37.200 --> 00:07:42.670
I was an emotional mess when Eichi
suddenly told me he was leaving.

00:07:44.500 --> 00:07:47.570
And the night before
Eichi left...

00:07:48.830 --> 00:07:52.970
<i>Tonight is the last time we sleep</i>
<i>under the same roof, Mitsuki.</i>

00:07:53.330 --> 00:07:54.400
<i>No...</i>

00:07:55.630 --> 00:07:59.300
<i>I want to be with you tomorrow night,</i>
<i>and the one after that.</i>

00:08:00.130 --> 00:08:01.130
<i>Mitsuki...</i>

00:08:05.400 --> 00:08:07.370
<i>It's not like we're going to</i>
<i>be separated forever.</i>

00:08:09.200 --> 00:08:13.430
<i>Until we make our dreams come true,</i>
<i>our time together is just going to stop.</i>

00:08:14.930 --> 00:08:19.100
<i>The next time we see each other,</i>
<i>our time will start to move again.</i>

00:08:20.370 --> 00:08:23.230
<i>Until then, I'll leave this</i>
<i>with you, Mitsuki.</i>

00:08:24.800 --> 00:08:26.670
It's been up there ever since that night.

00:08:28.030 --> 00:08:31.870
The time between Eichi and I
has stopped there.

00:08:32.400 --> 00:08:33.430
Is that so?

00:08:34.870 --> 00:08:37.100
<i>That's why she keeps</i>
<i>that old calendar.</i>

00:08:37.900 --> 00:08:40.500
Do you still talk with him?

00:08:40.930 --> 00:08:44.900
I don't know where
he moved to in America.

00:08:45.870 --> 00:08:49.500
Ms. Kazumi, do you know anything
about where he went?

00:08:50.170 --> 00:08:51.170
I'm sorry.

00:08:51.400 --> 00:08:54.100
I quit working at the orphanage
after getting married.

00:08:54.330 --> 00:08:55.330
I see.

00:08:57.530 --> 00:09:01.770
I know! I'll find him even if
I have to search all over America!

00:09:02.170 --> 00:09:03.300
Really?

00:09:03.570 --> 00:09:04.230
Oh, yes.

00:09:05.070 --> 00:09:09.470
You and Eichi will always be
my dear students.

00:09:09.630 --> 00:09:12.030
I'll do anything to help you!

00:09:12.070 --> 00:09:14.330
Thank you so much, Ms. Kazumi!

00:09:14.700 --> 00:09:15.970
Just leave it to me!

00:09:16.200 --> 00:09:20.070
Now we have someone who can help us!
Right, Takuto?

00:09:21.600 --> 00:09:24.830
So, what do you want to do
when you find Eichi?

00:09:24.870 --> 00:09:25.530
Huh?

00:09:25.570 --> 00:09:26.970
Since it's been two years,

00:09:27.000 --> 00:09:29.100
you must have tons of things
you want to tell him, right?

00:09:29.130 --> 00:09:31.100
Umm...

00:09:31.870 --> 00:09:32.900
I don't know.

00:09:33.930 --> 00:09:37.870
Well, then, think about it before
I go back to America.

00:09:38.130 --> 00:09:40.200
It's been a while, but it's
a homework assignment I'm giving you!

00:09:40.630 --> 00:09:41.300
Okay!

00:09:48.970 --> 00:09:50.970
<i>Maybe I'll find Eichi!</i>

00:09:51.600 --> 00:09:52.270
<i>And...</i>

00:09:52.770 --> 00:09:54.730
<i>Mitsuki, I like you.</i>

00:09:56.100 --> 00:09:59.100
<i>Then, I can finally tell him "I like you,"</i>
<i>which I couldn't back then.</i>

00:10:02.230 --> 00:10:05.870
<i>Oh, yes! I have to hurry and think</i>
<i>about Ms. Kazumi's assignment.</i>

00:10:06.670 --> 00:10:10.330
Did I serve a bad dish?

00:10:10.470 --> 00:10:12.500
I'm doing fine.

00:10:12.830 --> 00:10:13.900
Well, then...

00:10:14.400 --> 00:10:17.100
Mitsuki, why are you spacing out?

00:10:17.200 --> 00:10:18.370
Oh, yes!

00:10:19.230 --> 00:10:20.530
Thank you so much for dinner!

00:10:20.970 --> 00:10:24.630
W-Wait, Mitsuki, you're finished?
You barely touched anything!

00:10:26.200 --> 00:10:28.700
I'm sorry.
I have homework to do.

00:10:30.070 --> 00:10:31.730
Shall I write a letter?

00:10:32.430 --> 00:10:33.900
A letter?

00:10:33.930 --> 00:10:38.130
That's a great idea!
Letters are the most romantic!

00:10:38.170 --> 00:10:40.170
Yes! What should I write?

00:10:41.270 --> 00:10:41.930
What?

00:10:41.970 --> 00:10:44.400
Do you think I have to write in English?

00:10:45.800 --> 00:10:47.770
Of course Japanese is fine!

00:10:48.030 --> 00:10:49.600
Right. Good.

00:10:51.000 --> 00:10:53.070
I wonder how Eichi is doing.

00:10:53.100 --> 00:10:54.100
Let's see...

00:10:54.900 --> 00:10:58.500
What if Eichi has become way more
handsome than in this picture?

00:10:58.530 --> 00:11:00.470
I don't know what I'd do!

00:11:00.630 --> 00:11:03.900
I wonder if he'd think that
I've become prettier.

00:11:03.930 --> 00:11:06.070
Yes! He will! Of course he will!

00:11:06.100 --> 00:11:08.600
It's not like you're guaranteed
to find him, right?!

00:11:08.930 --> 00:11:12.370
I'll be able to see him for sure!
Ms. Kazumi will find him.

00:11:12.500 --> 00:11:16.070
In any case, it's not like
he'll be found today or tomorrow.

00:11:16.930 --> 00:11:17.930
What's wrong?

00:11:17.970 --> 00:11:21.970
Let's not even bother with guys that
don't understand girls' feelings!

00:11:22.370 --> 00:11:24.230
More importantly, the letter, the letter!

00:11:24.300 --> 00:11:24.970
Right!

00:11:25.700 --> 00:11:26.700
Do as you please!

00:11:26.830 --> 00:11:28.230
I'm fed up with this!

00:11:34.330 --> 00:11:35.530
<i>What's so great</i>
<i>about this Eichi?</i>

00:11:39.870 --> 00:11:44.700
<i>Well, this guy Eichi isn't just</i>
<i>a fantasy or an illusion.</i>

00:11:46.100 --> 00:11:49.070
<i>I'll find him even if I have to</i>
<i>search all over America.</i>

00:11:50.930 --> 00:11:52.600
<i>Surely, you'll find him someday.</i>

00:11:54.970 --> 00:11:57.300
Well, so what?!

00:11:57.930 --> 00:11:58.600
Stupid me.

00:12:13.930 --> 00:12:16.930
I see. You've decided
to write a letter?

00:12:17.170 --> 00:12:20.870
I thought of doing that and tried to do it
all night long, but couldn't really...

00:12:21.070 --> 00:12:22.570
What are you mad about?

00:12:22.870 --> 00:12:23.870
Nothing.

00:12:23.930 --> 00:12:26.630
I see. So that's why you came
to me seeking help.

00:12:26.770 --> 00:12:27.430
Yes!

00:12:27.470 --> 00:12:30.130
But I'm not sure if
I can be of any help.

00:12:30.430 --> 00:12:34.000
But you have such
a wonderful husband.

00:12:34.700 --> 00:12:35.700
You think so?

00:12:36.870 --> 00:12:39.370
How did you tell him your feelings?

00:12:39.770 --> 00:12:43.030
In my case,
I didn't use a letter, but that...

00:12:43.230 --> 00:12:43.900
Huh?

00:12:45.170 --> 00:12:46.800
A...video?

00:12:47.130 --> 00:12:49.400
That's right, I sent him a video-letter.

00:12:50.130 --> 00:12:51.900
More than writing a letter,

00:12:51.930 --> 00:12:56.000
I thought that sending the message directly
with words would convey more.

00:12:56.270 --> 00:12:57.300
I see!

00:12:57.400 --> 00:12:58.700
That's a great idea!

00:12:58.800 --> 00:13:02.770
That way, you can show Eichi
how you sing when you're Full Moon!

00:13:03.800 --> 00:13:06.770
Well, my story is just one example.

00:13:07.030 --> 00:13:10.530
No, that was so helpful.
Thank you so much!

00:13:12.470 --> 00:13:14.030
Ready... Start!

00:13:25.630 --> 00:13:29.130
Eichi, I've finally become a singer.

00:13:29.970 --> 00:13:33.700
I'm always singing to you across the sea.

00:13:33.970 --> 00:13:35.400
H-Hey! Stop !

00:13:35.930 --> 00:13:37.900
What are you doing, Takuto?

00:13:38.330 --> 00:13:40.700
Hey! Why are you interrupting this?!

00:13:40.730 --> 00:13:42.230
I don't like this at all!

00:13:42.370 --> 00:13:43.700
What are you talking about?

00:13:44.530 --> 00:13:47.500
Why are you in a bad mood?
Are you hungry?

00:13:47.530 --> 00:13:49.330
Stupid, it's not that.

00:13:49.370 --> 00:13:50.500
Well, then why?

00:13:51.330 --> 00:13:54.770
Nothing, really.
What I really want to say is—

00:13:55.170 --> 00:13:56.670
H-Hey! Let go of me!

00:13:56.700 --> 00:13:58.300
Alrighty, don't bother us now.

00:13:58.800 --> 00:14:02.100
Yes, yes, nothing gets done
when you mope around.

00:14:02.270 --> 00:14:04.200
That's your favorite phrase, right?

00:14:05.100 --> 00:14:06.100
How stupid.

00:14:08.270 --> 00:14:08.930
Huh?!

00:14:10.370 --> 00:14:11.370
Takuto!

00:14:11.500 --> 00:14:13.670
Hey, I can't film like this.

00:14:14.000 --> 00:14:15.730
I'm not going to help you anymore.

00:14:16.170 --> 00:14:17.170
But...

00:14:18.470 --> 00:14:20.370
Don't you think this is fake?

00:14:21.030 --> 00:14:22.670
Using that huge camera and all.

00:14:23.100 --> 00:14:24.900
If you really wanted to
deliver your message,

00:14:24.930 --> 00:14:27.200
shouldn't you show your true self?

00:14:27.970 --> 00:14:30.570
My...true self?

00:14:31.730 --> 00:14:33.630
Right! You're right!

00:14:33.970 --> 00:14:36.000
- If you got it, then...
- Thanks, Takuto!

00:14:36.200 --> 00:14:38.730
What?! Hey, wait!

00:14:39.430 --> 00:14:42.400
Jeez... Did she really get it?

00:14:43.370 --> 00:14:45.730
Oh, is this what you wanted?

00:14:45.770 --> 00:14:48.870
Yes. This one is better than
the ones at the TV station.

00:14:48.900 --> 00:14:50.600
Relax, Mitsuki.

00:14:51.700 --> 00:14:53.400
So she really didn't get it!

00:14:54.200 --> 00:14:58.170
Hey you, if all you're gonna do is complain,
can you please go away?

00:14:58.300 --> 00:14:59.330
All right.

00:14:59.600 --> 00:15:01.300
Okay, let's get started.

00:15:02.500 --> 00:15:03.770
Ready... Start!

00:15:04.370 --> 00:15:07.030
Eichi... Umm... How are you?

00:15:07.670 --> 00:15:11.630
No, you're too stiff!
Relax like you were before.

00:15:11.800 --> 00:15:14.970
When I'm not Full Moon,
I feel kind of shy.

00:15:15.130 --> 00:15:17.700
Just relax, relax.
Okay, here we go again!

00:15:17.970 --> 00:15:20.200
Eichi, how have you been?

00:15:20.330 --> 00:15:26.200
I couldn't tell you two years ago,
but I've liked you for so long!

00:15:26.230 --> 00:15:28.370
Hey! Are you taking this seriously?!

00:15:28.400 --> 00:15:30.930
You really like him, right?

00:15:31.070 --> 00:15:33.670
Then you've got to put
more feelings into it!

00:15:34.330 --> 00:15:36.170
But you told me to relax.

00:15:36.430 --> 00:15:40.030
That's way too relaxed!
Just be your normal self.

00:15:40.500 --> 00:15:43.130
You want to show how
you truly are, right, Mitsuki?

00:15:43.730 --> 00:15:45.900
Yes! Once more, please!

00:15:46.430 --> 00:15:48.100
I'm ready when you are!

00:15:53.030 --> 00:15:54.730
Eichi, I like you.

00:15:56.930 --> 00:16:02.200
Eichi, as we promised,
I am working hard to achieve my dreams.

00:16:03.230 --> 00:16:08.930
I was determined to become a singer,
and I went to an audition as Full Moon.

00:16:09.530 --> 00:16:13.530
Then, out of many applicants,
I was chosen.

00:16:14.100 --> 00:16:16.270
These days,
I have put out two albums,

00:16:16.300 --> 00:16:19.270
and I am participating in events
and performing at live shows.

00:16:20.130 --> 00:16:23.930
I'm very busy every day with TV
and radio shows too.

00:16:24.570 --> 00:16:28.330
I have fans that like my songs!

00:16:28.900 --> 00:16:31.970
Full Moon is pretty popular
at school too.

00:16:33.030 --> 00:16:36.670
<i>So that's how it's been,</i>
<i>working towards my dreams!</i>

00:16:36.970 --> 00:16:39.870
<i>Where are you,</i>
<i>and what are you doing now, Eichi?</i>

00:16:40.470 --> 00:16:42.400
<i>I want to see you soon!</i>

00:16:43.300 --> 00:16:46.970
<i>I'm waiting for our time together</i>
<i>to start moving again.</i>

00:16:47.870 --> 00:16:49.600
I'd say that's pretty good.

00:16:49.830 --> 00:16:50.500
Yes!

00:16:50.530 --> 00:16:53.570
Of course it is!
Because I directed it!

00:16:54.770 --> 00:16:59.300
Ms. Oshige, I want to give this video
to Ms. Kazumi.

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:02.370
Her flight to America takes off
at 1 p.m., right?

00:17:02.600 --> 00:17:04.470
If you leave now,
we can make it without a problem.

00:17:09.400 --> 00:17:10.070
Hey!

00:17:10.370 --> 00:17:11.970
Are you serious about delivering it?

00:17:12.270 --> 00:17:12.930
Huh?

00:17:13.300 --> 00:17:15.670
Hey, why are you still talking like that?

00:17:15.770 --> 00:17:20.230
For one thing, this video has the real Mitsuki
and Full Moon all mixed up, right?

00:17:20.530 --> 00:17:24.370
How can Eichi believe that
Mitsuki is Full Moon?

00:17:26.830 --> 00:17:28.970
I have to film the transformation too.

00:17:31.730 --> 00:17:33.170
Is that okay with you, Mitsuki?

00:17:33.700 --> 00:17:37.200
Yes... Eichi is so important to me.

00:17:38.000 --> 00:17:45.130
I want to tell him the truth,
like I told you and Dr. Wakaoji.

00:17:46.100 --> 00:17:49.130
You're right.
So, let's hurry and film that too.

00:17:49.400 --> 00:17:50.670
Takuto, please.

00:17:50.930 --> 00:17:51.600
I refuse.

00:17:51.800 --> 00:17:54.500
No way!
We came this far...

00:17:54.630 --> 00:17:57.470
Takuto! Just stop your nonsense now!

00:17:57.900 --> 00:18:00.800
Let me tell you this, you guys are
the ones that aren't making any sense!

00:18:01.030 --> 00:18:02.070
What do you mean?

00:18:02.770 --> 00:18:04.600
Mitsuki... Something's wrong with you.

00:18:05.230 --> 00:18:08.970
Didn't you decide to let Eichi find
you through your singing?

00:18:10.300 --> 00:18:14.800
I sympathized with that feeling and
helped you turn into Full Moon.

00:18:15.500 --> 00:18:17.570
You wanted him to notice you
through your singing,

00:18:17.600 --> 00:18:20.300
so shouldn't you keep your word
and go on working on that?

00:18:26.870 --> 00:18:28.170
Think about it.

00:18:29.800 --> 00:18:31.570
Hey, where are you going?

00:18:31.770 --> 00:18:32.770
Takuto!

00:18:39.000 --> 00:18:44.000
Yes...that's right.
Takuto is right.

00:18:45.170 --> 00:18:46.170
Mitsuki...

00:18:47.670 --> 00:18:50.230
What am I doing?

00:18:50.970 --> 00:18:55.700
Eichi wouldn't be happy
even if I sent this video to him.

00:18:56.530 --> 00:18:58.470
Don't you need to go to the airport?

00:18:58.830 --> 00:19:03.470
Isn't it better to give him
the video than to do nothing?

00:19:03.800 --> 00:19:06.670
Everything will stay the same if you don't.

00:19:06.870 --> 00:19:07.530
But...

00:19:07.930 --> 00:19:09.130
Let's go Mitsuki!

00:19:09.330 --> 00:19:10.800
There's no time to be indecisive!

00:19:19.500 --> 00:19:21.070
How is it? Can we make it?

00:19:21.300 --> 00:19:25.330
Traffic is kind of bad.
We might just barely make it.

00:19:47.400 --> 00:19:51.070
<i>Your father conveyed his feelings</i>
<i>through this one song, right?</i>

00:19:53.400 --> 00:19:55.830
<i>Why don't you try to follow</i>
<i>this example, shorty?</i>

00:20:05.270 --> 00:20:06.300
We made it.

00:20:06.930 --> 00:20:08.070
Come on, Mitsuki, hurry!

00:20:09.570 --> 00:20:11.000
What's wrong, Mitsuki?

00:20:11.230 --> 00:20:13.170
Ms. Oshige. Meroko...

00:20:13.500 --> 00:20:16.030
I am not going to hand over
this video after all.

00:20:16.300 --> 00:20:18.570
What are you talking about?!
We came all the way here!

00:20:19.100 --> 00:20:22.300
I'm sorry. But Takuto is right.

00:20:22.730 --> 00:20:26.570
I've decided to have Eichi notice me
through my songs.

00:20:27.170 --> 00:20:31.530
So I want to keep singing,
believing that he will one day notice me!

00:20:36.000 --> 00:20:37.670
Ms. Kazumi!

00:20:39.030 --> 00:20:40.030
Mitsuki!

00:20:42.800 --> 00:20:45.200
I'm glad I made it in time.

00:20:45.700 --> 00:20:51.800
Ms. Kazumi, if you find Eichi in America,
I want you to hand these to him.

00:20:52.200 --> 00:20:54.630
Huh? These?

00:20:54.830 --> 00:20:59.530
I think Eichi will understand once
he listens to those CDs.

00:20:59.770 --> 00:21:02.870
This is the answer to the homework
you gave me.

00:21:04.070 --> 00:21:06.130
I see. Okay.

00:21:06.570 --> 00:21:09.130
I'll hand these to him for sure,
so just hang on till I contact you.

00:21:09.670 --> 00:21:10.330
Okay!

00:21:11.200 --> 00:21:13.170
Good! Very well done.

00:21:19.830 --> 00:21:22.770
<i>Eichi... I'll sing...</i>

00:21:24.570 --> 00:21:29.330
<i>Believing that the day will come</i>
<i>when you'll notice me.</i>

00:23:06.600 --> 00:23:09.870
What?! Takuto!
You're all over Mitsuki again!

00:23:09.900 --> 00:23:14.130
I can't help it! She has a gig
at the university festival,

00:23:14.170 --> 00:23:16.630
and I have to protect her
as her bodyguard.

00:23:16.670 --> 00:23:19.900
Shut up! You're the worst!
You're so mean, Takuto!

00:23:19.930 --> 00:23:21.930
Meroko, calm down!

00:23:21.970 --> 00:23:24.500
Whatever. I'll do my own thing!

00:23:24.700 --> 00:23:28.230
You'll realize how great I am and apologize,
but it'll be too late!

00:23:28.900 --> 00:23:32.870
Next time on Full Moon:
"It's Autumn School Festival!"

00:23:33.330 --> 00:23:34.370
- Look forward to it!
- Look forward to it!
